      "writtenOn": "2022-06-01T18:18:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oof, that\u0027s so dicey. Where exactly are unsized arrays going to be allowed? I think this issue could go anywhere from \"not really that big a deal\" to \"we have to get this right\" depending on where unsized-array types are allowed to exist.\n\nI found at least two more potential problem areas:\n\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:external/skia/src/sksl/ir/SkSLConstructorCompound.cpp;l\u003d36-40;drc\u003dffba524ff800628fb550ba555157f3b2cde1d37e\n\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:src/sksl/codegen/SkSLVMCodeGenerator.cpp;l\u003d2174-2175;drc\u003d59c906795c50b54d7cdeebc167cfa377af28c7aa\n\nI don\u0027t have a good answer for what you should do instead but I don\u0027t think just returning 1 is a good idea. For a second I considered returning zero but that\u0027s even worse (this would let constant-folding checks pass that should fail).",
